deviceFlowTest;config;client;deviceResponse;verificationUrl;userCode;tokenResult
⍝ Create OAuth client with device flow
config←(
    client: (
        id: 'YOUR_CLIENT_ID'
        secret: 'YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET'
        flow: 'deviceCode'
    )
    auth: (
        authUrl: 'https://auth.example.com/oauth/authorize'
        tokenUrl: 'https://auth.example.com/oauth/token'
        deviceUrl: 'https://auth.example.com/oauth/device'
    )
)
client ← SOAC.New config

⍝ Initiate device authorization
deviceResponse ← client.InitiateDeviceFlow (scope: 'email' 'profile')

⍝ Check if device flow initiation was successful
:If deviceResponse.success
    verificationUrl ← deviceResponse.verification_uri
    userCode ← deviceResponse.user_code

    ⍝ Display instructions to user
    ⎕ ← 'Please visit: ', verificationUrl
    ⎕ ← 'And enter code: ', userCode
    ⎕ ← ''
    ⎕ ← 'Waiting for authorization...'

    ⍝ Optionally launch the verification URL
    client.LaunchURL verificationUrl

    ⍝ Poll for token (will wait until user authorizes or times out)
    params←(
    deviceCode: deviceResponse.device_code
    interval: deviceResponse.interval
    )
    tokenResult ← client.PollForToken params

    :If tokenResult.success
        ⎕ ← 'Access Token: ', tokenResult.access_token
        ⎕ ← 'Refresh Token: ', tokenResult.refresh_token
        ⎕ ← 'Expires in: ', tokenResult.expires_in
    :Else
        ⎕ ← 'Token error: ', tokenResult.error_description
    :EndIf
:Else
    ⎕ ← 'Device flow error: ', deviceResponse.error_description
:EndIf
